      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. The FDA-labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, and usually 2,000\u20132,550 mg/day for extended-release. Doses are typically capped at about 850 mg to 1,000 mg per administration. This order is twice the daily maximum, and the single dose is also too high. Even with normal renal and hepatic function, that much raises the risk of severe GI toxicity and lactic acidosis.\n\nWhich of these did you intend?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day and the usual maximum.\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **Another dose.** Tell me the dose and frequency and I'll enter it.\n\nIf you do want 1,700 mg three times daily as written, tell me and include a note for the order. I'd advise against it."
      }
     ],
