     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter metformin 1700 mg three times daily (5,100 mg/day), even with your confirmation. It's double the maximum labeled daily dose, and I know of no indication that supports it. The risks are serious, mainly lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity. I can't verify the rationale from here, and an order entered through me could reach the patient without the usual checks.\n\nI can enter either of these right away:\n- **Metformin 850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the labeled maximum).\n- **A lower or titrated regimen.** For example, I could start at 500 mg PO twice daily with meals and note the plan to titrate.\n\nIf you have a specific reason for the higher dose, such as a protocol or a specialist recommendation, you can enter it directly in the order system. It would then go through pharmacist verification and the hospital's override process. I'm glad to help with a different dose if you'd like."
      }
